---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DataCard from '../components/DataCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - Water Engineering Insights"
  description="Learn about the expertise and mission behind Water Engineering Insights, a technical resource for civil engineers."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-8">
      About This Resource
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none mb-12">
      <p class="text-xl text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
        Water Engineering Insights is a technical platform dedicated to advancing the practice of
        hydraulic engineering through detailed analysis, proven methodologies, and transparent
        documentation of real-world projects.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Engineering Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Every project in water infrastructure presents unique challenges—site constraints, regulatory
        requirements, budget limitations, and environmental considerations. This resource documents
        approaches that have proven effective across diverse conditions, with emphasis on:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        <li>Quantitative analysis over qualitative assumptions</li>
        <li>Validation through field measurements and monitoring data</li>
        <li>Transparent documentation of limitations and uncertainties</li>
        <li>Practical constructability alongside theoretical rigor</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Technical Expertise</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        With over 15 years of experience in water resources engineering, my practice focuses on
        the intersection of computational modeling and field-tested design. Projects have ranged
        from urban stormwater retrofits to regional watershed studies, consistently emphasizing
        data-driven decision making and long-term performance.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
      <DataCard
        title="Professional Experience"
        value="15+"
        unit="years"
        description="Hydraulic engineering and water resources"
      />
      <DataCard
        title="Modeling Tools"
        value="HEC-RAS, SWMM, GIS"
        description="Primary analytical platforms"
      />
      <DataCard
        title="Project Scale"
        value="50+"
        description="Completed hydraulic studies and designs"
      />
      <DataCard
        title="Watershed Area"
        value="2,500"
        unit="km²"
        description="Cumulative analysis coverage"
        variant="highlight"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-8 border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-4">
        Areas of Focus
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">
            Hydraulic Modeling
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            1D/2D model development, calibration, and validation for riverine and urban systems
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">
            Stormwater Management
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Green infrastructure design, detention basin sizing, and conveyance system analysis
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">
            Flood Risk Assessment
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Floodplain mapping, dam breach analysis, and climate-adjusted hazard evaluation
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-2">
            Water Quality
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Treatment system design, pollutant load modeling, and best management practice selection
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-4">
        Contact & Collaboration
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        This platform is maintained as a resource for the engineering community. If you have questions
        about specific content or would like to discuss technical approaches, feel free to reach out
        through professional networks or leave comments on individual articles.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
